WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:07.295
Ally crossed her fingers so tightly they were going numb as she waited for the robot to call out the winning number.

2
00:00:07.296 --> 00:00:09.918
"The winning number is 11!"

3
00:00:09.919 --> 00:00:13.965
"Ugh!" Ally collapsed back into her seat.

4
00:00:13.966 --> 00:00:17.648
"There goes my chance of getting back to space."

5
00:00:17.649 --> 00:00:21.012
"I'm so sorry," Mateo said.

6
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:29.190
She took a deep breath. "A good Astralian would be happy for the winner."

7
00:00:29.191 --> 00:00:35.945
She looked around the auditorium. "Where is number 11 anyway?"

8
00:00:35.946 --> 00:00:40.147
The auditorium buzzed as people double-checked their numbers.

9
00:00:40.148 --> 00:00:45.552
When no one claimed the prize, the robot said, "I will select a new number."

10
00:00:45.553 --> 00:00:48.881
"You have another chance!" Mateo said.

11
00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:52.743
The robot's lights flashed.

12
00:00:52.744 --> 00:00:59.648
Ally was wishing so hard, she didn't hear the robot call out the new number.

13
00:00:59.649 --> 00:01:05.414
But Mateo jumped up and started cheering. "You won, Ally! You won!"

14
00:01:05.415 --> 00:01:12.554
Stunned, Ally ran up to the podium, waving her winning number. "I'm going back to space!"

15
00:01:12.555 --> 00:01:15.810
As soon as the words came out, Ally covered her mouth.

16
00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:18.220
That's not what she meant to say at all!

17
00:01:18.221 --> 00:01:20.449
The audience burst out laughing.

18
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:24.365
As Ally looked out at them, she spotted the customer from the diner.

19
00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:29.039
She was sitting in the second row, a mysterious smile on her face.

20
00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:33.172
"It happened again!" she thought. "I blurted out the truth.

21
00:01:33.173 --> 00:01:40.258
That woman must be a Carparian! I'd better stay far, far away from her!"

22
00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:43.032
Ally gave the robot her name and address.

23
00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:46.374
Then the robot handed a printout to Ally.

24
00:01:46.375 --> 00:01:52.458
"These are your instructions. Follow them exactly or forfeit your prize."

25
00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:56.803
Ally stepped away from the podium, still shocked.

26
00:01:56.804 --> 00:01:59.188
Reporters began flocking around her.

27
00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:00.246
"What's your name?"

28
00:02:00.247 --> 00:02:04.258
"What did you mean when you said you're going back to space?"

29
00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:11.766
The questions were flying faster than an asteroid shower when the robot flashed its lights and made a new announcement.

30
00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.151
"There will be no questions and absolutely no photographs.

31
00:02:15.152 --> 00:02:21.272
If you do not obey this directive, Ms. Polk will never hold another press conference again."

32
00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:28.465
The reporters reluctantly backed away and made room for Ally and Mateo to exit the museum.

33
00:02:28.466 --> 00:02:32.962
Once they were back outside, Ally read the printout to Mateo.

34
00:02:32.963 --> 00:02:35.774
"'Get ready for the trip of a lifetime!

35
00:02:35.775 --> 00:02:41.979
Lainie Polk will send a car to your residence tomorrow morning to begin training for the flight. Good luck.'" "I

36
00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.944
can't believe I won!" Ally said. "I'm

37
00:02:44.945 --> 00:02:50.582
going back to space, and I'll get to meet Lainie Polk. I wonder what she's like." Mateo

38
00:02:50.583 --> 00:02:53.904
held up his phone. "I've been reading about her. She

39
00:02:53.905 --> 00:02:56.948
made her first million with an online store. She's

40
00:02:56.949 --> 00:03:02.878
very smart, and her knack for predicting new trends has earned her the nickname the Mind Reader." His

41
00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:08.133
phone beeped as a new text arrived. "Papi wants us to come to the diner." "Wait,

42
00:03:08.134 --> 00:03:12.876
they call Lainie Polk the Mind Reader?" Ally asked. "Mateo,

43
00:03:12.877 --> 00:03:17.077
she really might be a Carparian!" Mateo

44
00:03:17.078 --> 00:03:21.624
shrugged. "Or she might just be a good businesswoman. Don't

45
00:03:21.625 --> 00:03:25.906
worry. I won't let you be alone with her until we're sure." "Thanks,"

46
00:03:25.907 --> 00:03:33.706
Ally said. "That makes me feel a lot better." ***

47
00:03:33.707 --> 00:03:37.871
By the time they got back to the diner, it was closed for the day.

48
00:03:37.872 --> 00:03:41.373
Ray and Dawn were in the kitchen.

49
00:03:41.374 --> 00:03:46.146
"We're making a family dinner," Ray announced. "Can you kids please set a table?"

50
00:03:46.147 --> 00:03:50.342
As Ally and Mateo got to work, Ally watched Ray and Dawn.

51
00:03:50.343 --> 00:03:53.331
"They look so happy," she thought.

52
00:03:53.332 --> 00:04:00.799
"I guess getting them back together is one less thing I have to do before I leave Earth."

53
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.971
After they had finished eating, Ray clinked a spoon against his glass.

54
00:04:04.972 --> 00:04:11.139
"I have an announcement. I've been thinking about the diner lately. It's time for a change."

55
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:18.196
Ally gulped. Was Ray about to announce he was closing the diner so the family could move to the city?

56
00:04:18.197 --> 00:04:21.875
"I got a call from the bird-watchers' club today," Ray continued.

57
00:04:21.876 --> 00:04:25.963
"The male whooper was spotted flying through the desert with a stick in his beak.

58
00:04:25.964 --> 00:04:28.646
It's proof that the pair is building a nest.

59
00:04:28.647 --> 00:04:35.747
The bird-watchers will be camping out in the desert, searching for the nest, and they asked me to provide food for all their meals."

60
00:04:35.748 --> 00:04:41.974
"That's great, Papi," Mateo said. "But what's the change?"

61
00:04:41.975 --> 00:04:44.132
"I bought a food truck to make catering easier.

62
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:47.108
I'm going to call it Rolling Ray's.

63
00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:52.930
Now we can sell food at all kinds of events—fairs, rodeos, concerts.

64
00:04:52.931 --> 00:04:58.067
The sky's the limit!" Ray looked so excited, he was beaming like the sun.

65
00:04:58.068 --> 00:05:07.848
But across the table, Dawn crossed her arms, her face darkening like a thundercloud.

